  "aiContextParagraph": "The political alliance between the Congress party and the Samajwadi Party in Uttar Pradesh faces significant hurdles as seat-sharing negotiations continue to stall. Internal friction has emerged within the Congress ranks, with some leaders openly criticizing the Samajwadi Party's seat allocation offers. In response to public comments, Congress president M. Kharge has cautioned party members against displaying arrogance during the discussions. Simultaneously, the Samajwadi Party has moved forward by unveiling its election manifesto, which prioritizes the needs of youth, farmers, and rural households. The independent political figure Om Prakash Rajbhar has also joined the discourse, raising concerns regarding the Samajwadi Party's stance on law and order. These developments highlight the complex dynamics between the two parties as they prepare for the 2027 assembly elections in the region.",
